Subject: Cantor SJS Staged Diff Acquisition P1 Input Audit

@ [audit_uuid] c325a95f-5389-4a01-bf1d-347f6fcfb5f5
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] df917e83-5c3d-43d6-9308-a79d65583699

& [AuthorityAudit]
  + user continuation authorizes in-repository development and publication but does not erase SJS or source boundaries
  + P0 authorizes supplied-data verification only and explicitly requires a separate physical acquisition contract
  + current Git executable identity is evidence for one local experiment and not universal trust authority

& [CompatibilityAudit]
  + P1 may construct the existing DiffInventory without changing its profile or P0 verifier semantics
  + raw Git SHA-1 object IDs are locators only; DiffEntry before and after identities must be SHA256 of raw blob bytes
  + generated_refresh is not inferable from Git status and requires an exact operator-supplied staged modified path list

& [CriticalDelineation]
  + index observation is physical_contact true and observation_only
  + P0 graph verification remains physical_contact false and verification_only
  + Git mutation publication provider and self-signature remain absent

& [SelfReferenceFinding]
  + placing a machine ChangeSetManifest inside its own raw-content DiffInventory creates a cycle through inventory_sha256 and the staged change-set after_sha256
  + P1 must not claim to close commit-envelope self-reference
  + a future sidecar trailing-bookend or normalized governance-self-path policy requires separate source and SJS

& [Decision]
  + exact read-only acquisition receipt and DiffInventory production are SJS-ready
  + commit-hook integration and machine change-set self-custody are not part of this signature
